C) Both products need per-tenant parameterization regardless of whether customization is  
   actually required, since it's best practice to always build for future flexibility.
D) The distinction is irrelevant to application design, since customization only affects the  
   user interface layer, never the prompt or model configuration.

### Q2.19 · Configuration Management *(select TWO)*
A mid-sized engineering org manages five Claude-powered internal tools, each maintained by a  
different team, each with its own model version pin, its own prompt version history, and its  
own plugin dependencies — currently tracked inconsistently: some in a spreadsheet, some only  
in each team's memory. Which two changes would most improve configuration management here?

