regardless of which individual employee is actually using the tool, with no per-user  
identity carried through to determine what that specific person is authorized to see or do.

A) This is acceptable as long as the shared service account itself has a strong,  
   non-expiring credential.
B) This collapses individual authorization into a single shared identity, making it  
