times within seconds, driving up cost and occasionally tripping the tool's own rate limits,  
because nothing in the harness or prompt currently caps repeated identical calls.

A) A system-prompt instruction telling the model "don't retry the same failing call more  
   than twice" is a fully reliable way to prevent this, since the model will consistently  
   comply once told.
B) A hook that deterministically detects and blocks (or backs off) repeated identical tool  
   calls within a short window is the appropriate enforcement mechanism — a runaway retry  
   loop is exactly the kind of pattern that shouldn't depend on the model's own in-context  
   judgment holding under every circumstance.
C) The fix is to remove the failing tool from the agent's toolset entirely rather than  
